{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.md","line":441,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives.tex","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint","line":912,"source":"\\begin{definition}[adjoint of the covariant derivative]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-adjoint}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0077}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor}\n\n  For an $(s,t)$-tensor $S$ with $t>0$, and an orthonormal frame\n  $E_1,\\dots,E_n$, the \\emph{adjoint} $\\nabla^*S$ is the $(s,t-1)$-tensor\n  \\[\n    (\\nabla^*S)(X_2,\\dots,X_t)=-\\sum_i(\\nabla_{E_i}S)(E_i,X_2,\\dots,X_t).\n  \\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[adjoint of the covariant derivative] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368322d636f76617269616e742d646572697661746976652d61646a6f696e74\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0077</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_Derivatives%23def%3Apet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor\">↗ def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor</a> <p></p>For an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(s,t)$\">$(s,t)$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t&gt;0$\">$t&gt;0$</span>, and an orthonormal frame <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E_1,\\dots ,E_n$\">$E_1,\\dots ,E_n$</span>, the <em>adjoint</em> <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\nabla ^*S$\">$\\nabla ^*S$</span> is the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(s,t-1)$\">$(s,t-1)$</span>-tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  (\\nabla ^*S)(X_2,\\dots ,X_t)=-\\sum _i(\\nabla _{E_i}S)(E_i,X_2,\\dots ,X_t).  \\]\">\\[  (\\nabla ^*S)(X_2,\\dots ,X_t)=-\\sum _i(\\nabla _{E_i}S)(E_i,X_2,\\dots ,X_t).  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-hessian-covariant-derivative","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor","label":"def:pet-ch2-covariant-derivative-tensor"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","title":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula","label":"prop:pet-ch2-divergence-adjoint-formula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity","title":"prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity","label":"prop:pet-ch2-adjoint-integral-identity"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-hessian-second-covariant-derivative","title":"rem:pet-ch2-hessian-second-covariant-derivative","label":"rem:pet-ch2-hessian-second-covariant-derivative"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_Derivatives#rem:pet-ch2-ex-34","title":"rem:pet-ch2-ex-34","label":"rem:pet-ch2-ex-34"}],"copy_co